<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tamanrasset</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tamanrasset is the main town of the Ahaggar region in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. It grew from a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> settlement and a French military post of the early 20th century, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-foucauld">Charles de Foucauld</a> lived from 1905. It is now a provincial capital and a stop on the trans-Saharan route.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tamanrasset.jpg" alt="Tamanrasset" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Habib kaki · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cour_d%27assises_de_Tamanrasset_%D9%85%D8%AC%D9%84%D8%B3_%D9%82%D8%B6%D8%A7%D8%A1_%D8%AA%D9%85%D9%86%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%B3%D8%AA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
